{"title":"1982 IMO Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1982_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/f/eef0203e65664bd00b5f0325c5c5fcd81bcead8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"38\" height=\"20\" /> is defined on the positive integers and takes non-negative integer values. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/6/a36ab597ca78885fa75e891ca28e94ba428c708f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(2)=0,f(3)&gt;0,f(9999)=3333$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"275\" height=\"20\" /> and for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/3/5d373bdf104b138edd283c54a11b0a582d81d9dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m,n:$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"11\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/7/6c7a65eeb658762fe0cc9161175eaaedaf1993f2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(m+n)-f(m)-f(n)=0 \\text{ or } 1.\\]\" width=\"266\" height=\"18\" />Determine <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/1/4318b2aff52f57580742871270521ba46b364e55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1982)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1982_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Clearly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/7/9276fcbd5c39ad3b1fa7b1aa642e5fa800bb225a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1) \\ge 1 \\Rightarrow f(m+1) \\ge f(m)+f(1) \\ge f(m)+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"385\" height=\"18\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/3/5838b22f97e6393b787daff17a17d3cab1551995.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(9999) \\ge 9999$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"121\" height=\"18\" />.Contradiction!So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/d/89d358367015e5ceeb10a72c78d0b627d586f3ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" />.This forces <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/f/25f478ffd3bc5a2cdbac17fecf17e8a519f0b571.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(3)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" />.Hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/1/ce18fbaa6d2611aa360e31d0d85754f6e4ff3975.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(3k+3) \\ge f(3k)+f(3)&gt;f(3k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"267\" height=\"18\" /> so the inequality <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/4/fd462426772d23f7afb3495b8ad888f7cef1d386.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(3)&lt;f(6)&lt;\\cdots&lt;f(9999)=3333$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"283\" height=\"18\" /> forces <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/1/d51a9b4c6a39a099d1a1163f6764009c6dc278ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(3k)=k \\forall k \\le 3333$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"158\" height=\"18\" />.Now <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/f/1cf99d2028c40bbbf9ae46c87e4946563b2b50bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(3k+2) \\ge k+1 \\Rightarrow f(6k+4) \\ge 2k+2 \\Rightarrow f(12k+8) \\ge 4k+4 \\le f(12k+9)=4k+3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"690\" height=\"18\" />(Note:This is valid for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/c/e3c7a03897439be31fbfb170db63cdd2d512c5e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12k+9 \\le 9999$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"119\" height=\"15\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/7/9979e5b5abd4dd63da226b4a0c2040965df6dd03.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3k+2 \\le 2499$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"110\" height=\"15\" />).Contradiction!Hence the non-decreasing nature of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/b/b4bc051b43a97ce4d12c12ce1c93016f5769f469.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(3k+1)=k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"109\" height=\"18\" />.Hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/b/84b3e2f5f1490c472c8bc3949c05ee19b8f6f9ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n)=\\lfloor\\frac{n}{3}\\rfloor \\forall 1\\le n \\le 2499$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"208\" height=\"34\" />.\n</p><p>So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/d/12deb2f1654fe33e4a6309fbc83cf42683a0176a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1982)=\\lfloor\\frac{1982}{3}\\rfloor=660$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"193\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>This solution was posted and copyrighted by sayantanchakraborty. The original thread for this problem can be found here: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"https://aops.com/community/p3472764\">[1]</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1982_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First observe that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/7/b272cfcb0611913ea0be06e9967097c5cf21f848.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3333=f(9999)\\geq f(9996)+f(3)\\geq  f(9993)+2f(3)\\geq \\cdots\\geq 3333f(3)\\]\" width=\"536\" height=\"18\" />Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/3/003fdb0d6edace39b9ce3789476864e120619656.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> is a positive integer, we need <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/f/25f478ffd3bc5a2cdbac17fecf17e8a519f0b571.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(3)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" />. Next, observe that\n\\begin{align*}\n3333=f(9999)\\geq 5f(1980)+33f(3)=5f(1980)+33\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad f(1980)\\leq 660\n\\end{align*}On the other hand, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/b/6cb405e8b58224334648afdd76c149c748f7a455.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1980)\\geq 660f(3)=660$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"197\" height=\"18\" />, so combine the two inequalities we obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/c/2ecc37e669f64577b95b886248d0d25a42bc40ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1980)=660$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"112\" height=\"18\" />. Finally, write\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/0/6d069654495750203544d4a928c30446b1979c81.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(1982)=f(1980)+f(2)+0\\vee 1=660\\vee 661\\]\" width=\"361\" height=\"18\" />Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/f/3ff216f26b2fcdca448f6238f604dff420173234.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1982)=661$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"111\" height=\"18\" />, then\n\\begin{align*}\n3333=f(9999)\\geq 5f(1982)+29f(3)=3305+29=3334\n\\end{align*}a contradiction. Hence we conclude that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/6/eb6b95608b3b6dd8e68ee6730d336dd6b759daf3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1982)=660$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"112\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>This solution was posted and copyrighted by Solumilkyu. The original thread for this problem can be found here: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"https://aops.com/community/p6118061\">[2]</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1982_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/8/9d8f5ceb7dc65f9bc8369c145c08a00e12745958.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n) = [n/3]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"97\" height=\"18\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/a/1aa949042b3f50add690f7a3c61e7dfa49e4c17a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n &lt;= 9999$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"85\" height=\"13\" />, where [ ] denotes the integral part. We show first that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/9/b09797e3051f5001b2df9230daea3a8d74cfce18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(3) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/5/bb5b19bf7575fdc3655bb5767980f09dbb747a8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, otherwise <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/2/1e25bff1ca836d3cf7d7831eff3580ce23ea47e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(2) - f(1) - f(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"145\" height=\"18\" /> would be negative. Hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/2/bc26d9198950ba78b857b4ba2e58fe845c511416.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(3) = f(2) + f(1) + 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"179\" height=\"18\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. But we are told <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/0/8609382fdb45b118e48c0755312d3ed73ab85fbd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(3) &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/9/b09797e3051f5001b2df9230daea3a8d74cfce18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(3) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" />. It follows by induction that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/1/8318803054503e6e22eddabc2d71714431fa74d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(3n) &gt;= n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"94\" height=\"18\" />. For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/c/dfc171310a3adeebf074fa39db488cf849d9c640.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(3n+3) = f(3) + f(3n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"200\" height=\"18\" /> + <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/a/24a9a6c9ae4b79f792bb8b6b41022b3064741020.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 = f(3n) + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"108\" height=\"18\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Moreover if we ever get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/0/35065d3080db7c76015eb50745e0d8b2c19af47f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(3n) &gt; n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"18\" />, then the same argument shows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/6/cb66decf79315b8f8a44b69564f561534a47eeaa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(3m) &gt; m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"90\" height=\"18\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/0/2b0b58b81ad8d1281aaf0c31d8bf23d6e26cf24e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m &gt; n$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"50\" height=\"10\" />. But <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/a/25ac8301e2cc41911e45d735513bbc01af914eaf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(3.3333) = 3333$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"135\" height=\"18\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/d/97d240a3e49a25f89bcf604d0c125d790f891679.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(3n) = n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"18\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/b/7db1d110ea9a8e210719002c97d0061d9c3d18e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n &lt;= 3333$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"85\" height=\"13\" />. Now <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/1/f81ad7a0248b80977e096884bbaf1c19092d87ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(3n+1) = f(3n) + f(1) + 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"232\" height=\"18\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/5/ac5429dc4aa7ba1f3b20be4599a34c4220cc79db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" />. But <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/1/5716f1af5ce1b5726e1bdc3e7327da3daede9b79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3n+1 = f(9n+3) &gt;= f(6n+2) + f(3n+1) &gt;= 3f(3n+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"487\" height=\"18\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/8/4e874dcaf5ff5fea2343c8dc0aae805556662751.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(3n+1) &lt; n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"141\" height=\"18\" />. Hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/c/13c50d00934201026b9a4b97db4aaf4b1445115c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(3n+1) = n.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"115\" height=\"18\" /> Similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/a/b6a8ca105989c446cc1a21a025c7823036f8b2ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4f(3n+2) = n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"120\" height=\"18\" />. In particular <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/9/a49965f4b6d01ab86744e2d270b67ffbca96ed7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1982) = 660$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"115\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>This solution was posted and copyrighted by Tega. The original thread for this problem can be found here: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"https://aops.com/community/p6118103\">[3]</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1982_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Similar to solution 3.\n</p><p>Proof:\nLemma 1: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/6/fd688b8a3c092ef9f31e5c0d4edb7ed59400bf95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(mn)\\geq nf(m)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"126\" height=\"18\" />\nLet, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/2/f82f7fff64f3892c02b03c42fe9bd2ed76f1110b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(m,m)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" /> be assertion.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/6/5a615cf83eb6d3ebbaa4132d22201d91129cf2e4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(2m) \\geq 2f(m)\\]\" width=\"122\" height=\"18\" />Similarly,we can induct to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/3/cd34fd3d7a16b51ca9215e30e6c829a96180db85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(nm)\\geq nf(m)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"126\" height=\"18\" />.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/e/d5e2f7d2da26745687dec97db0264982e0445b3e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(3m) \\geq f(2m)+f(m) \\geq 3f(m)\\implies f(nm)\\geq \\underbrace{f(m(n-1))+f(m)\\geq .....}_{\\text{n times}}\\geq nf(m)\\]\" width=\"663\" height=\"41\" />Lemma proved.\n</p><p>Then we see that,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/7/0c775ef399ac4b4627e0b831f28fb907b4e8eb18.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(9999)\\geq 3333f(3) \\implies f(3)=1:f(3)&gt;0\\]\" width=\"354\" height=\"18\" />Then,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/5/bb5cdfb37625b1b441518a39bc0d32aec77053fb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(9999) \\geq 5f(1980)+33f(3) \\implies 3300 \\geq 5f(1980) \\implies f(1980) \\leq 660\\]\" width=\"564\" height=\"18\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/f/94faf9feefe5eb4d61d8c14689fe81375243737c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(1980) \\geq 660f(3) \\implies f(1980)=660\\]\" width=\"308\" height=\"18\" />Then we can easily get,by assertion <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/6/2365e069a4c87567a7e2728484f455f9f9bd54b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(1980,2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/0/2b04131cb134297a204a891ab3214d937314ee9a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(1982)=660 \\space or \\space f(1980)=661\\]\" width=\"241\" height=\"18\" />Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/c/b4cccf630b379ed672f1152b326246fc9ebcc0df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{f(1980)=660,661}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"160\" height=\"29\" />.And, we are done. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>This solution was posted and copyrighted by IMO2019. The original thread for this problem can be found here: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"https://aops.com/community/p10482615\">[4]</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1982_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/d/03d7776b252204c30a8b73a3126d0cc65fb8bac8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(m+n) - f(m) -  f(n) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"231\" height=\"20\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/c/29c622248a899513a4903df732b03c6ddec47611.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(kn) = kf(n) + a(k,n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"193\" height=\"20\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/5/df54598ffb51d805d80fed445a558a0f75d18ab9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a(k,n) \\in \\{0,...,k-1\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"177\" height=\"20\" />. Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/6/db6b0ea26248b77287d00855d6a7257de47ee0b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n) = \\Big\\lfloor\\frac{1}{k}f(kn) \\Big\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"141\" height=\"38\" />, i.e. \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/7/967c42838e230d2286b9f4448ae3c29f2227ad07.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f\\Big(\\frac{n}{k}\\Big) = \\Big\\lfloor\\frac{1}{k}f(n) \\Big\\rfloor \\text{ if } k|n. \\ \\ \\ \\ \\ (1)\\]\" width=\"240\" height=\"37\" />\nFurthermore, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/a/0caf0902a1a0ceaec280f223237c2e023ae87e91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2|m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"65\" height=\"20\" /> then \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/6/7f604b65aeaa7f00d4cd1a617876154a2a3e8662.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f\\Big(\\frac{m+n}{2}\\Big) = \\Big\\lfloor \\frac{1}{2}f(m+n) \\Big\\rfloor = \\Big\\lfloor \\frac{1}{2}\\Big(f(m)+f(n)\\Big) \\Big\\rfloor. \\ \\ \\ \\ \\ (2)\\]\" width=\"445\" height=\"37\" /> \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/9/0d9c3b1c142cbd3f8217dabc160c57e4750df241.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> will allow us to find smaller values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> from larger values, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/f/62f62a19f0425d8e6121ca0c1cfd3ce96e43c9c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> allows finding larger values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> from smaller values.\n</p><p>Applying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/9/0d9c3b1c142cbd3f8217dabc160c57e4750df241.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/9/68958c6cb2ce825f2feac733b09410bb7b3632fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(9999) = f(3^2 \\cdot 11 \\cdot 101)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"201\" height=\"21\" /> yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/1/a315ca5109a23d9d4821a6caa9c8cebccd60d18b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(9999/k) = \\Big\\lfloor\\frac{1}{k}f(n) \\Big\\rfloor =  \\Big\\lfloor\\frac{9999}{3k} \\Big\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"259\" height=\"38\" />. Applying this,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/a/2aaaac50923588edad3b50cc2a9acad1f468ed84.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}  f(3333) &amp;= 1111 \\\\ f(1111) &amp;= 370 \\\\  f(303) &amp;= 101 \\\\ f(101) &amp;= 33 \\\\ f(99) &amp;= 33. \\end{align*}\" width=\"120\" height=\"117\" />\nIn order to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/1/4318b2aff52f57580742871270521ba46b364e55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1982)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"18\" /> we will successively find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/0/86049601391d56d9ab858e8e436832f98ea79b68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(100), f(202), f(151), f(631)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"235\" height=\"20\" /> and then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/1/4318b2aff52f57580742871270521ba46b364e55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1982)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"18\" />. By <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/f/62f62a19f0425d8e6121ca0c1cfd3ce96e43c9c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> and the equations above for particular values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" />,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/6/116e437cb06b9adc2e5af5bd48a311e1da35ddf7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}  f(100) &amp;= f\\big((99+101)/2\\big) = \\Big\\lfloor \\frac{1}{2}\\Big(f(99)+f(101)\\Big) \\Big\\rfloor = 33, \\text{ also,} \\\\ f(202) &amp;= f\\big((101+303)/2\\big) = \\Big\\lfloor \\frac{1}{2}\\Big(f(101)+f(303)\\Big)\\Big\\rfloor = 67, \\text{ hence,}  \\\\   f(151) &amp;= f\\big((100+202)/2\\big) = \\Big\\lfloor \\frac{1}{2}\\Big(f(100)+f(202)\\Big)\\Big\\rfloor = 50, \\text{ hence,} \\\\  f(631) &amp;= f\\big((151+1111)/2\\big) = \\Big\\lfloor \\frac{1}{2}\\Big(f(151)+f(1111)\\Big)\\Big\\rfloor = 210, \\text{ hence,}  \\\\   f(1982) &amp;= f\\big((631+3333)/2\\big) = \\Big\\lfloor \\frac{1}{2}\\Big(f(3333)+f(631)\\Big)\\Big\\rfloor = 660. \\end{align*}\" width=\"552\" height=\"209\" />\n</p><p>~not_detriti\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1982_IMO\" title=\"1982 IMO\">1982 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1982_IMO_Problems\" title=\"1982 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First Question</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1982_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1982 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1982_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1982 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1982_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1982 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1982_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1982 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1982_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1982 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1982_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1982 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017141516\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.046 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.059 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 460/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 868/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 52/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 18330/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.597      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    7.597      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:20532:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017141516 and revision id 278251. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}